*HEADING
A3s: the A3 crossing as SOLID cylinders (C3D8R, structured O-grid): A (r 0.8, along x, L 10) with both end faces clamped; free B (r 0.5, along y) 0.3 mm above, 2 m/s down; frictionless general (surface-to-surface) contact; linear elastic E0; reference for radius-aware contact (vs our A3 beams). v2: 16x16 O-grid, surface-biased radial layers, axial slices graded to 0.03 mm at the crossing, enhanced hourglass control (v1 had 65% of its internal energy in hourglass modes)
** Generated by abaqus/cases.py (O-grid: 16x16 centre + 4 x 16x5 blocks per section,
** axial size 0.25 mm). Units: mm, N, s, tonne, MPa. Solid contact uses the true surfaces (no beam radius).
